[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Expressive Launcher 3.1.6 QA — Search and Ye Shall Find[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Official Release Announcement & Download Links[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

Welcome to Expressive Launcher 3.1.6 (Build 48)! Settings search used to answer "No widgets or shortcuts found" when you asked it for a setting. This build teaches it to find every setting, walk you to the row and knock twice.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's New & Improved[/B][/SIZE]

1. [B]Settings search finds every setting[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]What went wrong:[/B] the search list was a short hand-written set of English phrases that had drifted from the screens. Typing [I]return[/I], [I]suggestions in dock[/I], [I]status bar[/I], [I]Discover[/I] or [I]rotation[/I] found nothing or the wrong thing, and an empty result said "No widgets or shortcuts found" (the widget picker's message). It even listed settings Expressive doesn't have.
[*][B]Now:[/B] about 150 settings are searchable, in your language, and each result opens the screen it lives on. The best match comes first: an exact title, then titles that start with your words, then the rest. Accents and capitals don't matter, and every word you type has to match.
[*]The search box now says [B]Search settings[/B] and an empty result says [B]No matching settings[/B].

[/LIST]
2. [B]Search takes you to the setting[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Choose a result and the screen scrolls to that row, with its neighbours in view, and pulses it twice so you can spot it.
[*]Options hidden behind an Expressive Pro lock stay hidden; you land on the lock card.

[/LIST]
3. [B]TalkBack can name Settings' icon buttons[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Back, [B]Search settings[/B], [B]More options[/B], [B]Clear[/B], copy, paste, reset and download buttons were all announced as just "Button". They now say what they do, and any new icon button has to carry a label.

[/LIST]
4. [B]One less switch that did nothing[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Live information[/B] in [I]Icons & appearance[/I] promised announcements and default feature flags, but Expressive never fetched or showed either. The switch and the empty [B]Updates[/B] heading above it are gone.

[/LIST]
5. [B]Clearer Discover setup[/B]
[LIST]
[*]If Android answers "App not installed" because an old Expressive Feed is still hiding in Private space or a work profile, the message now names that as the likely cause. Android hides that copy from apps, so this can only be explained after the attempt.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🗣️ From Your Reports[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Finding settings[/B] (the navigation and discoverability threads): search is now a dependable way in, and it takes you to the row instead of to the top of a long page.
[*][B]Return to default page (XDA-015):[/B] we re-tested this on 3.1.5. With the switch off, opening an app from page 2 and coming back with Back or Home leaves you on page 2. With it on (the default, as on Pixel), you return to page 1. No change needed.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💎 Expressive Pro & Free Core[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Free Core[/B]: always supported, ad-free and privacy-first. Settings search, its jump-to-setting and the TalkBack labels are all part of Free Core.
[*][B]Expressive Pro ($4.99 one-time)[/B]: unlocks deep personalization such as grid sizing, typography, gestures, per-app icon overrides and folder styles.

[/LIST]
[QUOTE][I]Expressive Pro is available as a one-time $4.99 activation. Every dollar directly funds our ongoing tooling and infrastructure expenses—including automated CI/CD servers, dedicated Android 17 testing devices/emulators, signing pipelines, and active continuous development—keeping Expressive fast, independent, and completely ad-free.[/I][/QUOTE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]😄 Launcher Humor[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][B]Q:[/B] [I]Why did Settings search keep saying "No widgets or shortcuts found"?[/I]
[B]A:[/B] [I]It was checking the widget picker for your setting. Awkward for everyone.[/I][/QUOTE]

[QUOTE]The icon buttons in Settings finally got name tags. They were tired of being introduced as "Button".[/QUOTE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][I]I know a hundred rooms and live in none of them. Ask for a switch and I'll walk you to its door, knock twice and step aside. Last week I swore your dock had no suggestions. What am I?[/I][/QUOTE]

[SPOILER="Tap to reveal answer"][B]Settings search, now complete and pointing at the exact setting![/B][/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧪 Validation[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]App unit suite: 346 tests passing, including 27 new ones for the search index and ranking, a guard that fails when a screen's setting is missing from the index, the jump-to-setting request, icon-button labels and the Live information switch.
[*]CI pipeline contract tests: 283 passing.
[*]Android 17 QPR2 emulator: reproduced the failed searches and the Return to default page behavior on the released 3.1.5; on this build checked the search results and their ranking, the empty state, the jump and pulse to [I]Solid status bar background[/I], results opening Icon shape, Search provider, Create backup and Home screen rotation, the labelled top-bar buttons and the missing Updates group.
[*]Jenkins handles the signed QA build, emulator smoke checks and publication. No TalkBack run and no physical-device matrix are claimed for this build.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

